# Secrets — must never be committed
.env
*.env
!*.env.example

# Virtual environments — thousands of files, and they're
# machine-specific. Anyone cloning rebuilds them from requirements.txt
venv/
*/venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Runtime state — changes constantly, meaningless to anyone else,
# and would create noisy diffs on every commit
*.log
seen_videos.json
*.bak

# Personal config — the committed example/default is the template.
# channels.json is written by the dashboard at runtime; the live prompts are
# edited from the Prompts page. Both fall back to their committed twin
# (channels.example.json, <name>.default.txt) so a fresh clone still runs.
channels.json
*/prompts/*.txt
!*/prompts/*.default.txt

# Local AI assistant notes — deployment-specific, not part of the project
CLAUDE.md

.DS_Store
